# Angular Unit Testing Conventions

## Ionic Overlay Controllers — DI Override Issue

`ModalController`, `PopoverController`, `AlertController`, `LoadingController` are Ionic overlay controllers. Ionic's root provider **may win over TestBed's provider**, meaning `{ provide: ModalController, useValue: spy }` is NOT reliably injected into the component.

**Always** directly assign the spy to the component property after creation:

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — works even when Ionic overrides TestBed provider
(component as any).modalController = modalCtrlSpy;

// ❌ UNRELIABLE — TestBed provider may be overridden by Ionic root
providers: [{ provide: ModalController, useValue: modalCtrlSpy }]
```

Do this in `beforeEach` immediately after `fixture.detectChanges()`:

```typescript
beforeEach(waitForAsync(() => {
  modalCtrlSpy = jasmine.createSpyObj('ModalController', ['create', 'dismiss']);
  TestBed.configureTestingModule({ ... }).compileComponents();
  fixture = TestBed.createComponent(MyComponent);
  component = fixture.componentInstance;
  fixture.detectChanges();
  // Directly replace to bypass Ionic DI override
  (component as any).modalController = modalCtrlSpy;
}));
```

See `achievement-pop-up.component.spec.ts` for the canonical example.

## NgZone and ChangeDetectorRef in Direct-Constructor Tests

When tests instantiate components directly (`new MyPage(...)`) rather than via TestBed, every constructor parameter must be passed explicitly. For `NgZone` and `ChangeDetectorRef`, use these inline mocks:

```typescript
component = new MyPage(
  serviceSpy,
  // ...other deps...
  { markForCheck: jasmine.createSpy('markForCheck') } as any,  // ChangeDetectorRef
  { run: jasmine.createSpy('run').and.callFake((fn: () => any) => fn()) } as any, // NgZone
);
```

The `NgZone` mock must call `fn()` synchronously via `callFake` so that subscription callbacks wrapped in `ngZone.run(() => {...})` execute immediately in tests.

## Why NgZone.run() Is Used in Production

Components use `this.ngZone.run(() => { ...; this.cdr.markForCheck(); })` inside subscription callbacks to ensure change detection fires correctly in browser contexts (Cypress, Playwright). Do not remove this pattern.
